# The output of `ops/id.sh`. It holds this restaurant's org/branch/device ids AND its three
# shared secrets, so it is the one file in this repo that must never be committed. `id.sh`
# also chmods it 600; this entry is the second lock, because a `git add -A` from an
# orchestrator that shares this working tree would otherwise capture it (AGENTS.md records
# that exact accident on a different path).
ids.env

# Backup output, if an operator points `ops/backup.sh` here instead of at a real destination.
backups/
